2026-07-28T06:37:18.7413168Z [36;1m# standard flags R selects per version (e.g. -std=gnu2x for C, -std=gnu++17[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7413692Z [36;1m# / -std=gnu++20 for C++); a plain "CC = ccache gcc" override would drop[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7414181Z [36;1m# them and silently downgrade the standard across the version matrix.[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7414681Z [36;1m# Inference uses an empty user Makevars so we always read the pristine[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7415113Z [36;1m# Makeconf defaults, never a value we just wrote.[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7415545Z [36;1m# Note: the versioned switches (CXX11..CXX23) intentionally come out as[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7416024Z [36;1m# bare "g++" with no -std flag. R keeps the standard in a separate[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7416502Z [36;1m# CXXnnSTD variable (CXX17STD = -std=gnu++17, ...) and applies it on top[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7417011Z [36;1m# at compile time, so wrapping only CXXnn with ccache is correct and we[0m
2026-07-28T06:37:18.7417423Z [36;1m# must NOT pin -std here ourselves.[0m
